[0.424, "o", "Here's a Python validator for Bangladeshi mobile numbers. It accepts the local `01XXXXXXXXX` format and the international `+8801XXXXXXXXX` / `8801XXXXXXXXX` forms, with optional spaces, dashes, or parentheses.\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "```python\r\nimport re\r\n\r\n# Mobile: 01[3-9] + 8 digits (11 digits total locally)\r\nBD_MOBILE_RE = re.compile(r\"^(?:\\+?880|0)1[3-9]\\d{8}$\")\r\n\r\ndef is_valid_bd_phone(number: str) -> bool:\r\n    \"\"\"Return True if `number` is a valid Bangladeshi mobile number.\"\"\"\r\n    cleaned = re.sub(r\"[\\s\\-()]\", \"\", number)\r\n    return bool(BD_MOBILE_RE.match(cleaned))\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "...\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
